WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.580
Too expensive, bad scripts, and a legacy nobody
wants to touch.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.040
In sci-fi, anything is possible…except a
sequel to these films.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:15.500
Tom Cruise is no stranger to sci-fi, having
starred in films such as Minority Report and

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.860
Edge of Tomorrow.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.779
One that is often overlooked, however, is
2013's Oblivion.

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:27.680
Directed by Joseph Kosinski, Oblivion thoughtfully
explores ideas of isolation, love, and survival.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.040
Not only is the movie visually stunning, but
it also includes the supporting talents of

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:37.710
Olga Kurylenko, Nikolaj Coster-Waldau, and
Morgan Freeman, and features a breathtaking

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.620
soundtrack composed by the French electronic
band M83.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:46.786
Cruise plays Jack Harper, a technician who
lives on a remote base in a post-apocalyptic world.

00:00:46.786 --> 00:00:51.560
He and his partner, Victoria, played by Andrea
Riseborough, are seemingly the only humans

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:56.469
on Earth and are tasked with protecting the
ruins of the planet from alien scavengers.

00:00:56.469 --> 00:01:00.649
Harper believes that he and Victoria will
rejoin the remaining human colonists on Saturn's

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:02.879
moon once they have completed their objective.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:08.229
However, as they go forward with their task,
Harper begins to quest ion who and what he

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:11.270
is, and if what he and Victoria are doing
is right.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:16.414
"I don't know what happened, but you're not
who you think you are."

00:01:16.414 --> 00:01:20.360
Oblivion does leave us with lots of questions
that could be expanded upon.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.619
It's the kind of story that would really lend
itself to a prequel.

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:28.580
It would be interesting to see a film explore
how the war-ravaged Earth ended up this way,

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.619
and what Harper's life was like beforehand.

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:35.150
With Cruise still in great shape — and the
advancements of de-aging technology — a

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:38.369
prequel with the same cast wouldn't be out
of the question.

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:44.759
In the 2018 sci-fi film Upgrade, Grey Trace,
played by Logan Marshall-Green, is a mechanic

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:47.900
living in a futuristic world run by technology.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.299
One day, he and his wife are attacked when
their hi-tech car malfunctions.

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:57.257
The thugs murder Grey's wife, and he is left
as a quadriplegic following damage to his spine.

00:01:57.257 --> 00:02:02.290
Not helped by the trauma of what happened,
the previously anti-tech Grey suddenly becomes

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:07.399
completely reliant on it when he signs up
to be a test subject for an experimental technology

00:02:07.399 --> 00:02:08.920
to help him walk again.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.750
It works…but with some unintended side effects.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.080
"I need your permission to operate independently."

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.118
"Permission granted."

00:02:16.118 --> 00:02:17.078
"Thank You."

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.720
Upgrade shows what someone is capable of doing
when they're left with no choice, and the

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.810
film's ending leaves plenty of room for more
exploration.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.920
The experiment leaves Grey as an overpowered
supercomputer with no empathy for humanity,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.860
and this offers so much opportunity for a
sequel or franchise.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.680
The good news is the filmmakers agree, and
Deadline announced in 2020 that director Leigh

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:45.770
Whannell and producer Jason Blum were turning
the movie into a television series.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:50.500
Set a few years after the events of the film,
the series will focus on a new host, as well

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:56.042
as the ways that the government is using evolved
technology to deal with criminals and illegal activity.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:59.430
It might not be an easy road to getting the
series made, however.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:04.310
In 2021, Blum told Collider that the first
scripts didn't make the grade, saying,

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:07.730
"We're working on the scripts again, so that
we can get an order."

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:12.090
Since then, news has gone quiet about the
state of the project, but hopefully, it'll

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.450
get off the ground soon.

00:03:13.671 --> 00:03:18.700
Directed by Josh Trank, Chronicle was a surprise
critical success and box office hit when it

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.247
was released in 2012.

00:03:20.247 --> 00:03:24.950
The found-footage film takes the idea of a
superhero's origin story and flips it on its

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:30.900
head to tell us a villain's origin story instead
— delivering a film that is heartfelt, suspenseful,

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.090
and even uncomfortable at times.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:37.060
Andrew Detmer, played by Dane DeHaan, is a
high school student who gets bullied by his

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.780
peers and father.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:43.400
One day he — along with his cousin Matt,
played by Alex Russell, and popular jock Steve,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:48.000
played by Michael B. Jordan — stumbles across
a meteor that gives them telekinetic powers.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:53.090
At first, they use their abilities to enhance
their lives, however, as Andrew's suffering

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.640
grows, so does his need to take power.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:00.480
Consumed by rage, he begins to see himself
as an apex predator and believes everyone

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.950
else is beneath him and should be destroyed.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:06.910
Chronicle ends with Matt promising Andrew
that he'll do good works with his gifts.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:10.000
But now that the world has seen their powers,
what will Matt do?

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.879
And how will Andrew's actions and death haunt
Matt into his adult life?

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:15.530
Only a sequel can answer that.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:20.235
While screenwriter Max Landis had penned a
sequel, Trank didn't want to move ahead with it.

00:04:20.235 --> 00:04:21.841
The director told Polygon,

00:04:21.841 --> 00:04:24.950
"I really didn't ever want to see Chronicle
2 happen.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.850
That was my worst nightmare."

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:30.780
Unless he has a change of heart, a follow-up
seems very unlikely.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:35.948
Sci-fi series Firefly was something of a cult
hit when it was released, with Rotten Tomatoes

00:04:35.948 --> 00:04:39.670
even naming it as the 12th best sci-fi series
of all time.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:45.320
But the western themed space opera was unceremoniously
canceled after just one season in 2002.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:49.800
Fortunately, the story picks up with the 2005
film Serenity.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:53.871
The movie follows the same ragtag group of
outcasts on the Serenity spaceship, whose

00:04:53.871 --> 00:04:58.389
lives get upended when River Tam, played by
Summer Glau — a woman with psychic powers

00:04:58.389 --> 00:05:00.780
and a strange past — hides on board.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:05.910
Unfortunately, not enough people watched it,
so the studio vetoed any more talk of sequels.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:10.410
While diehard Firefly fans have been calling
out for more big-screen adventures for years,

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.000
they are yet to materialize.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.676
Star Nathan Fillion told Entertainment Weekly,

00:05:14.676 --> 00:05:19.280
"If I got $300 million from the California
Lottery, the first thing I would do is buy

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:23.440
the rights to 'Firefly,' make it on my own,
and distribute it on the Internet."

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.007
"So no more running.

00:05:28.007 --> 00:05:30.161
I aim to misbehave."

00:05:30.161 --> 00:05:34.690
In a later interview with Esquire, Fillion
said that this comment "accidentally rallied

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:38.120
the troops," as fans started raising money
for him to get the rights.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:42.470
Going forward, he intends to be more careful
giving voice to his pipe dreams.

00:05:42.615 --> 00:05:48.220
Audiences are used to seeing Tom Cruise play
the dashing hero, but 2014's Edge of Tomorrow

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:51.620
offers something new: The character he plays
is a bit of a coward.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:56.690
Cruise plays PR officer, Major William Cage,
a man reluctantly thrust into a raging war

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:00.470
between humans and a seemingly unbeatable
race of aliens.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:03.639
"Says here you're a deserter.

00:06:03.639 --> 00:06:06.319
Says here you were caught impersonating an
officer."

00:06:06.319 --> 00:06:10.900
At one point in a battle, Cage gets infected
with alien blood just before dying.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:16.599
He miraculously wakes up 24 hours prior, seemingly
the only person with memories of his time

00:06:16.599 --> 00:06:17.890
on the battlefield.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:22.750
It's Groundhog Day meets an alien invasion
story, as Cage dies repeatedly in combat.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:27.699
Forced to relive the same battle, he eventually
becomes a better fighter under the tutelage

00:06:27.699 --> 00:06:32.760
of Emily Blunt's Sergeant Rita Vrataski, who
had previously held the same ability.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:38.220
Talk of the next chapter of Edge of Tomorrow
began almost immediately and in 2016, director

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:41.669
Doug Liman told Collider that he had plans
to do a prequel.

00:06:41.669 --> 00:06:46.009
In 2019, Entertainment Weekly confirmed that
an Edge of Tomorrow prequel was in development

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:50.970
at Warner Brothers but just two years later,
it ironically seemed to be stuck in a loop.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:55.440
Emily Blunt told Entertainment Weekly in 2021
that she had read the treatment for Edge of

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.729
Tomorrow 2, saying,

00:06:56.729 --> 00:07:01.030
"It was an amazing script, but I just don't
know what the future holds for it."

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:02.699
"Honestly, I think the movie's too expensive."

00:07:03.324 --> 00:07:09.389
Robert Zemeckis' 1997 feature Contact, based
on Carl Sagan's novel of the same name, follows

00:07:09.389 --> 00:07:14.310
Dr. Ellie Arroway, played by Jodie Foster,
a communications specialist who finds proof

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.759
of alien life.

00:07:15.759 --> 00:07:19.699
Tasked with going to space in order to make
first contact with them, the journey challenges

00:07:19.699 --> 00:07:22.289
her in ways she never anticipated.

00:07:22.289 --> 00:07:25.979
Contact is a layered, philosophical story
that just happens to be sci-fi, as well.

00:07:25.979 --> 00:07:29.590
It's not a big blockbuster action flick like
Independence Day.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.449
Instead, it offers a slow build that leaves
you questioning the nature of life and what

00:07:33.449 --> 00:07:35.639
it means to make true connections.

00:07:35.639 --> 00:07:39.393
"They should have sent a poet.

00:07:39.393 --> 00:07:41.173
So beautiful."

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:47.150
Jodie Foster is not an actor who likes to
do sequels — she famously passed on reprising

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:51.389
her role as Clarice in the sequel to Silence
of the Lambs — unless the plot is exactly

00:07:51.389 --> 00:07:52.599
what she wants.

00:07:52.599 --> 00:07:57.190
Since Contact is a movie she holds very close
to her heart, a sequel is unlikely.

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:59.810
Carl Sagan died while the film was in production.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.150
Speaking to Vulture about him, Foster said
that,

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:06.589
"To be responsible in a way for the legacy
of Carl Sagan is really amazing to me.

00:08:06.589 --> 00:08:09.300
That feels just like a really big deal in
my life."

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.889
"Until I sat down with Carl, I don't think
I really thought much about the vastness of

00:08:13.889 --> 00:08:14.889
the universe."

00:08:14.889 --> 00:08:17.980
A sequel to Contact isn't totally out of the
question.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:22.789
Co-screenwriter Michael Goldenberg told Vulture
that he has a pitch for a limited series,

00:08:22.789 --> 00:08:25.099
but so far, nothing has come from that.

00:08:25.099 --> 00:08:30.290
Christopher Nolan likes to take audiences
on unexpected journeys, and his 2010 sci-fi

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.450
film Inception does just that.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:36.210
The film plays around with dreams and how
they can be powerful motivators.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:40.159
Although much of Inception feels like a heist
film, the story is ultimately about the lengths

00:08:40.159 --> 00:08:42.830
a father will go to in order to be with his
family.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:47.610
Leonardo DiCaprio plays Dom Cobb, a man wrongly
accused of murdering his wife.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:51.760
"Do the children miss me?"

00:08:53.462 --> 00:08:55.639
"I can't imagine."

00:08:55.639 --> 00:08:59.500
To avoid arrest, he fled the country and hasn't
seen his children since.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:04.269
Cobb works as an "extractor," using experimental
dream technology to infiltrate a person's

00:09:04.269 --> 00:09:07.519
subconscious to extract information for his
clients.

00:09:07.519 --> 00:09:12.450
When businessman Mr. Saito asks him to commit
to an impossible job and promises he can finally

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:15.890
return home to his children if he pulls it
off, Cobb agrees.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:18.420
The ending of Inception is deliberately ambiguous.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:23.221
Audiences never find out if Cobb is in the
real world with his kids or still in the dream world.

00:09:23.221 --> 00:09:26.794
While it is an audacious way to end a film,
we'd love to learn more.

00:09:26.794 --> 00:09:28.598
What about the rest of the characters?

00:09:28.598 --> 00:09:31.358
If Cobb is trapped in a dream, how will it
affect them?

00:09:31.358 --> 00:09:32.887
What happens if he wakes up?

00:09:33.089 --> 00:09:38.670
Based on the book by Andy Weir, Ridley Scott's
2015 film The Martian stars Matt Damon as

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.870
botanist Dr. Mark Watney.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:45.060
After finding himself stranded on Mars, Watney
is tasked with trying to survive while NASA

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.589
works on a rescue mission to bring him back
home.

00:09:47.589 --> 00:09:53.140
Set in the year 2035, this sci-fi film offers
a fresh take on the genre, with a focus on

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:56.580
pure survival rather than the discovery of
alien creatures.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:10:04.770
"In the face of overwhelming odds I'm left
with only one option: I'm gonna have to science

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:05.770
the s— out of this."

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:09.410
The biggest challenges Watney faces are finding
and rationing basic necessities like food

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:12.070
and water and trying to maintain his sanity.

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:16.890
The Martian was loved by audiences and critics
alike and it was nominated for a total of

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:20.660
seven Oscars, but it's unlikely that a sequel
will materialize.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:25.640
However, the rights to Andy Weir's follow-up
novel Artemis, described as "an adrenaline-charged

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:30.080
crime caper," have been acquired by 20th Century
Fox and New Regency.

00:10:30.792 --> 00:10:36.370
Akira imagines a post-apocalyptic world in
which Tokyo has become Neo-Tokyo, a dark place

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:38.570
filled with violence and corruption.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:43.190
Shotaro Kaneda is the leader of a motorcycle
gang who discovers a group of people with

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:47.831
telekinetic powers living in Neo-Tokyo as
well as others who want to use that power

00:10:47.831 --> 00:10:49.000
for their own means.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:54.279
Akira introduces a bleak and violent world,
but one that is also thought-provoking and challenging.

00:10:54.279 --> 00:10:58.829
Since its release, it's been the subject of
hyperbolic praise, with Dazed declaring it,

00:10:58.829 --> 00:11:01.187
"The most important animation of all time."

00:11:01.187 --> 00:11:05.100
While there have been numerous attempts to
turn Akira into a live-action movie — with

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:10.040
Warner Bros. first acquiring the rights in
2002 — so far, nothing has emerged.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:13.899
The story presents a number of challenges,
but that's not to say people aren't trying

00:11:13.899 --> 00:11:15.029
to bring it back.

00:11:15.029 --> 00:11:19.400
Taika Waititi was the most recent director
tipped to do the live-action remake, but his

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:22.040
plans got pushed so he could do the Thor movies.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:26.080
In 2021, Waititi told Wired he still wants
to do the film, saying:

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.311
"I'm still trying.

00:11:27.311 --> 00:11:28.820
[...] I don't wanna give up on that."

00:11:29.185 --> 00:11:33.820
Steven Spielberg's Ready Player One, adapted
from the Ernest Cline novel, brings together

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:37.950
nostalgia, pop culture, and a hugely enjoyable
adventure story.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:42.880
In a dystopian future, people find solace
in the virtual reality game called "OASIS."

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:45.570
In the game, you can be whoever and whatever
you want.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:50.060
Wade Watts is a lonely teenager who goes by
the name of "Parzival" in OASIS.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:53.899
When the founder of the game dies, it's announced
that whoever can solve a puzzle and find the

00:11:53.899 --> 00:11:56.700
golden key will become the new owner of the
game.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.399
"If you're watching this, I'm dead."

00:11:59.399 --> 00:12:03.519
Wade is determined to win and embarks on a
treasure hunt that takes him to places he

00:12:03.519 --> 00:12:04.457
never dreamed of.

00:12:04.457 --> 00:12:09.230
By the film's end, Wade makes a decision regarding
OASIS that changes the course of every single

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:11.089
person's life on the planet.

00:12:11.089 --> 00:12:15.120
It's such a huge moment, and we'd love to
see what the repercussions of his decision

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.279
have on humanity.

00:12:16.279 --> 00:12:20.940
Fortunately, a sequel to the novel, Ready
Player Two, was released in 2020, although

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.460
it was universally panned by critics.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:28.029
Cline told Inverse that the feature film adaptation
of Ready Player Two is in the early stages

00:12:28.029 --> 00:12:31.810
of development but time will tell whether
it will make it to the big screen given the

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:33.500
novel's poor reception.

00:12:33.865 --> 00:12:38.980
As the debut feature from writer and director
Andrew Niccol, Gattaca is a pretty impressive

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.070
first offering.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:45.010
The movie stars Ethan Hawke, Uma Thurman,
and Jude Law, and is a thoughtful exploration

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:49.600
of the meaning of life in an advanced society
that uses genetics to determine a person's

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:50.709
place in the world.

00:12:50.709 --> 00:12:54.779
In the not-so-distant future, parents are
able to splice together the best part of their

00:12:54.779 --> 00:12:58.000
genes to make a genetically superior child.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.839
Anyone that's born the old-fashioned way is
considered to be inferior and given a lower

00:13:01.839 --> 00:13:04.060
standing in society because of it.

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:07.570
Hawke portrays Vincent Freeman, one of those
unlucky children.

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:12.770
He meets the genetically superior Jerome Eugene
Morrow, played by Jude Law, a former Olympic

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.890
athlete who's become paralyzed.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:18.620
The two decide to cheat the system, and Vincent
pretends to be Jerome.

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:23.940
"They won't believe that one of their elite
could have suckered them all this time."

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:28.680
With his now superior standing, Vincent gets
a job working at Gattaca as a navigator for

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.630
a space project to Saturn's moon.

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:35.262
The film ends with Vincent being allowed to
keep Jerome's life, and he leaves for his mission.

00:13:35.262 --> 00:13:39.129
What happens to him and the world that's been
introduced is anyone's guess, but a sequel

00:13:39.129 --> 00:13:43.760
— or even a prequel — could explore the
moral implications of genetic advances and

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:46.959
what it means for the people who get left
behind because of it.

00:13:46.959 --> 00:13:50.459
Unfortunately, Niccol seems to have closed
the door on a sequel project.

00:13:50.459 --> 00:13:52.139
In an interview with Fandom, he said,

00:13:52.139 --> 00:13:54.291
"I don't know that there needs to be a sequel.

00:13:54.291 --> 00:13:56.547
Once you've said it, do you need to say it
again?

00:13:56.547 --> 00:13:58.202
We'll leave it to your imagination.

00:13:58.202 --> 00:14:01.497
Better that you write the sequel in your mind
than I write it."

00:14:01.891 --> 00:14:07.389
Starring Sigourney Weaver, Alan Rickman, and
Tim Allen, Galaxy Quest is a sci-fi cult classic

00:14:07.389 --> 00:14:09.529
that everyone needs to experience.

00:14:09.529 --> 00:14:13.101
While on the surface it looks to be a film
that just pokes fun at Star Trek, it really

00:14:13.101 --> 00:14:14.509
is so much more than that.

00:14:14.509 --> 00:14:19.060
It's a fun story about how fame and fortune
can ruin relationships, and sometimes you

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:22.240
just need a quick trip around the universe
to make things right again.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:26.139
The film follows a group of actors from the
canceled sci-fi show, Galaxy Quest.

00:14:26.139 --> 00:14:30.730
For the most part, the cast can't stand the
show's original lead — Jason Nesmith, played

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:31.730
by Tim Allen.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:35.310
However, when a group of aliens abducts the
cast — believing what they've watched to

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:39.940
be fact rather than fiction — the actors
face the biggest challenge of their careers:

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.300
Being actual heroes.

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:42.700
"This is great.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:45.689
You know, usually it's just cardboard walls
in a garage."

00:14:45.689 --> 00:14:50.190
Star Trek is a franchise that seems to run
and run, so it is only right that Galaxy Quest

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:53.980
should receive the same treatment, especially
as the film ends with the cast getting their

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:54.980
show renewed.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:15:00.200
Collider reports that Amazon Prime is poised
to revive Galaxy Quest as a television series,

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:04.480
however, following the tragic passing of Alan
Rickman, they paused their plans.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:09.139
Weaver shares that if the revival series does
move forward, it will focus on a younger Galaxy

00:15:09.139 --> 00:15:13.750
Quest cast joining forces with the remaining
original cast members for another adventure

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:14.750
in space.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:20.933
When you talk about cult-classic sci-fi films,
no list is complete without 1997's The Fifth Element.

00:15:20.933 --> 00:15:25.459
The film stars Milla Jovovich's as Leeloo
— the embodiment of the titular fifth element

00:15:25.459 --> 00:15:30.223
— who must combine herself with the other
elements to stop "The Great Evil" from destroying everything.

00:15:30.223 --> 00:15:34.870
Luckily, she falls into the cab of New Yorker
Korben Dallas, and he helps her on her journey

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.060
to save the world.

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:40.620
In many ways, The Fifth Element could be considered
as hugely ahead of its time, a sentiment with

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.970
which director Luc Besson agrees.

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:47.100
Besson points out that not only was the movie
more comedy than action, but it also had a

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:49.279
woman as the primary action star.

00:15:49.279 --> 00:15:53.800
This combined with the outlandish costumes
designed by Jean-Paul Gaultier, and the decision

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:58.690
to have one of the main characters unable
to speak English, made the film a hard sell.

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:02.029
Audiences didn't quite know what to make of
it, and this was reflected in its disappointing

00:16:02.029 --> 00:16:06.019
initial box office figures, which put a stop
to any talk of a sequel.

00:16:06.019 --> 00:16:10.320
However, given audiences' receptiveness to
the weird and wonderful, and the subsequent

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:14.269
cult status of The Fifth Element, a sequel
would likely be welcome.

00:16:14.269 --> 00:16:18.449
Just because Leeloo and Dallas saved the planet
once, doesn't mean that they can't do it again.

00:16:18.449 --> 00:16:21.509
"What doesn't kill you makes you stronger."

00:16:21.961 --> 00:16:27.449
Directed by Christopher Nolan, 2014's Interstellar
explores the possibilities of wormholes, time

00:16:27.449 --> 00:16:29.980
displacement, and above all else, family.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:33.630
It's an emotional tale of a father who leaves
his children in the hopes of giving them a

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.690
better life.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:38.579
With food running out and the planet growing
closer to mass-level extinction, Earth can

00:16:38.579 --> 00:16:43.459
no longer sustain humanity and so an alternative
place to live must be found.

00:16:43.459 --> 00:16:51.529
"Find us a new home, and by the time you return,
I will have solved the problem of gravity."

00:16:51.529 --> 00:16:55.960
Matthew McConaughey plays single dad, Cooper,
who is tasked with leading a team to find

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.540
a new habitable planet.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:02.551
While Interstellar tells a beautifully poignant
story, it ultimately has a sad ending for Cooper.

00:17:02.551 --> 00:17:06.380
When he eventually gets back home after many
years have passed, his young daughter is on

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:07.390
her deathbed.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:13.140
"Nobody believed me, but I knew you'd come
back."

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:17.449
Interstellar ends with Cooper leaving once
more to find his mission partner, Dr. Amelia

00:17:17.449 --> 00:17:21.570
Brand, who is still traveling alone in space
somewhere with no idea about what happened

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:23.130
to Earth and humanity.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:27.420
A story about their adventures would be an
intriguing tale, especially after the success

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.730
that Interstellar enjoyed upon its release.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:34.330
While doing the press tour for Interstellar
in 2014, McConaughey told Sky News that a

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:37.980
sequel was possible, but nothing has come
of it yet.

00:17:38.365 --> 00:17:43.539
E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial is one of pop culture's
defining sci-fi films, from the director who

00:17:43.539 --> 00:17:46.919
has made a number of such films in his career,
Steven Spielberg.

00:17:46.919 --> 00:17:51.970
With the perfect blend of nostalgia, whimsy,
and effective storytelling, E.T is the blueprint

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:55.130
of how to make a successful family-friendly
sci-fi movie.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:18:00.330
The film tells an emotional tale about a young
boy, Elliott, and his new alien friend, E.T.,

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:02.440
who finds himself stranded on Earth.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:05.650
The two form a beautiful bond that transcends
species.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:09.659
They connect over their shared experience
of feeling separate from their families.

00:18:09.659 --> 00:18:12.070
Most of the adult characters in the film react
to E.T.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:16.400
with fear and suspicion, but Elliott recognizes
the gentleness and good in him.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.850
The film ends with E.T.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:21.500
going home — which is his mission from the
beginning — but there is heartbreak on both

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.880
sides when he has to say goodbye to Elliot.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:28.040
While the idea of seeing these beloved characters
in another feature would be welcome, it feels

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:31.870
like, if a sequel were going to come to light,
it would've happened already.

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:36.120
Following the success of E.T., the studio
did push the idea of a follow-up, but nothing

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:37.179
came of it.

00:18:37.179 --> 00:18:41.289
Speaking to Slash Film about the possibility
of a sequel, actor Henry Thomas said:

00:18:41.289 --> 00:18:42.919
"I think it should be left alone."

00:18:42.919 --> 00:18:48.389
A reunion of sorts took place in 2019 featuring
some of the original cast — including Thomas

00:18:48.389 --> 00:18:51.510
— reuniting with the lovable alien for a
holiday commercial.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:53.460
The former child star went on to say,

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:57.930
"I think the commercial was as close as we're
going to get to a sequel and that's why Spielberg

00:18:57.930 --> 00:18:58.930
okayed it."

00:18:59.238 --> 00:19:04.039
What Galaxy Quest does for Star Trek, Spaceballs
does for Star Wars, offering an exceptionally

00:19:04.039 --> 00:19:07.130
goofy take on the familiar tropes of the iconic
franchise.

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:11.200
While occasionally brutal in the way it pokes
fun at some of the more ridiculous plot points

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:15.040
in Star Wars, Spaceballs is a film that doesn't
take itself too seriously.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:18.980
Its loving, carefree approach to its pastiche
is irresistibly charming.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:24.250
The film follows the kidnapping of Princess
Vespa, who is being held hostage by Dark Helmet.

00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:28.340
The Darth Vader-esque baddie holds her for
ransom in the hope of obtaining air, as his

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:30.450
planet has depleted its air supply.

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:35.200
Fortunately, she is rescued by bad boy space
pilot Lone Starr and his half-man, half-dog

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.470
partner, Barf.

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:40.909
Many fans of the film assumed that another
story was in the works, especially after Spaceballs

00:19:40.909 --> 00:19:43.570
teased various titles for sequel films.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.309
However, nothing has come out yet.

00:19:45.309 --> 00:19:50.580
At a Q&amp;A event in 2017, Mel Brooks talked
about the possibility of doing another film,

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:53.730
especially since the first movie became a
cult classic.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:58.210
Unfortunately, as many of the original cast
members have now passed away, any new stories

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:02.820
would need to feature a new cast and be told
in a way that would honor those who came before.

00:20:03.128 --> 00:20:09.150
While technically, Dredd is a reboot of the
1995 film Judge Dredd starring Sylvester Stallone,

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:13.760
the 2012 film bears very little resemblance
to the previous movie and they appear to be

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:15.990
connected in name and title character only.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:20.700
As the only film in its particular universe,
2012's Dredd earns a place on this list.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:25.679
In a dystopian city called Mega-City One,
the judges have the power to act as judge,

00:20:25.679 --> 00:20:26.929
jury, and executioner.

00:20:26.929 --> 00:20:32.230
Dredd, played by Karl Urban, takes rookie
Cassandra Anderson, played by Olivia Thirlby,

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:35.530
with him to a 200-story apartment to investigate
a murder.

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:39.929
The building is controlled by a violent drug
lord named Ma-Ma, played by Lena Headey.

00:20:39.929 --> 00:20:43.510
She's a formidable foe, but she meets her
match in Judge Dredd.

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:50.636
"But as for you, Ma-Ma, judgment time."

00:20:50.636 --> 00:20:55.290
Critics praised Dredd and fans have turned
it into a cult classic, but the movie failed

00:20:55.290 --> 00:21:00.790
to recoup its $50 million budget with a meager
worldwide haul of $41 million.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:05.470
While the 2018 comic Dredd: Final Judgment
is an official sequel to the film, we have

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:07.760
yet to see anything new on-screen.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:12.620
Olivia Thirlby expressed her enthusiasm for
a Dredd sequel, telling Collider in 2021,

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:16.640
"I was always the number one advocate of getting
a sequel for Dredd.

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:20.670
[...] If there is still talk of there being
a sequel 10 years later, I am all for it."

00:21:20.875 --> 00:21:26.299
2002's Minority Report has an incredible amount
of talent both in front of and behind the

00:21:26.299 --> 00:21:31.010
camera, with Tom Cruise in the leading role
and Steven Spielberg in the director's chair.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:35.850
Cruise plays Chief John Anderton, the commanding
officer of the Precrime Unit, an experimental

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:39.460
prototype program designed to stop murders
before they happen.

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:43.570
Initially, John wholeheartedly believes in
Precrime, until he witnesses a murder that

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:45.330
he's about to commit in the future.

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:49.750
Once John starts investigating, he uncovers
damaging evidence regarding the supposedly

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:51.100
fool-proof unit.

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:55.700
The premise for Minority Report is instantly
engaging, and it feels like a story that could

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:58.508
expand into a franchise or multiple installments.

00:21:58.508 --> 00:22:04.007
"I'm sorry John, but you're going to have
to run again."

00:22:04.007 --> 00:22:08.570
The Precrime unit uses the special abilities
of three humans called "precogs," who have

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:12.250
the ability to see the future and witness
crimes before they happen.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:16.220
With their skills proven to be fallible, it
opens up a number of questions about them

00:22:16.220 --> 00:22:17.830
that a sequel could address.

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:22.760
One of the rare exceptions on this list, Minority
Report was brought back as a television show,

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:24.320
airing in 2015.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:29.080
The story takes place a little over 10 years
after the film and follows one of the precogs

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:31.260
who still retains their ability.

00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:35.580
Unfortunately, the series was canceled by
Fox after just one season, but there's still

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:38.150
room for the story to continue on the big
screen.

